      up: {"title":"High-key, low-key or motivated? (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>These lighting plans are described in technical terms. Sort each by its MAIN approach, using the key-to-fill ratio and the logic of the light source as your clues.</p>","items":[{"t":"A morning-show set lit with large soft panels, so the fill is almost as bright as the key.","bin":0,"fb":"A low key-to-fill ratio gives faint shadows: high-key."},{"t":"An interrogation scene with one hard overhead light and no fill; the walls fall into darkness.","bin":1,"fb":"No fill and deep shadows: low-key."},{"t":"A night scene in a car where the only visible glow seems to come from the dashboard, created with a small hidden LED.","bin":2,"fb":"The light imitates a believable source in the scene: motivated."},{"t":"A beach-resort advert where large reflectors bounce sunlight into every shadow.","bin":0,"fb":"Filling every shadow makes the look bright and even: high-key."},{"t":"A thriller in which the detective's face is half in shadow, lit hard from one side, with the rest of the frame near black.","bin":1,"fb":"A high contrast between light and deep shadow is low-key."},{"t":"A reception scene where a hidden warm lamp is placed to look as if the table candles are lighting the guests.","bin":2,"fb":"The crew controls the light, but the audience believes the candles are the source: motivated."},{"t":"A bank's corporate video with bright, even light on white walls and no harsh shadows on the staff.","bin":0,"fb":"Even, low-contrast light: high-key."},{"t":"A noir-style music video for a Kingston artiste, with striped shadows from window blinds and deep blacks.","bin":1,"fb":"Hard shapes of shadow and deep blacks are the classic low-key noir look."},{"t":"A classroom scene in which a soft light outside the window, angled like late-afternoon sun, is the only key light.","bin":2,"fb":"The window is the believable source: motivated light."}],"win":"Well analysed. The key-to-fill ratio separates high-key from low-key, while motivated lighting is defined by a believable source in the story world, whatever its brightness."}
