      up: {"title":"Which typefaces for a bank and a carnival poster? (Challenge)","bloom":"Evaluate","q":"<p>The Kingston designer's clients now want screen versions. The bank needs a <b>mobile banking app</b> that shows balances and transactions in small type. The carnival fete needs a <b>vertical TikTok promo</b> with text over moving footage. Which typeface plan is MOST appropriate for both?</p>","options":[{"t":"App: the same carnival display face as the poster, so the two clients' brands match.","fb":"These are different clients with different messages, and a display face is illegible at small sizes."},{"t":"App: a high x-height sans serif at 16 px or more, with lining numerals of equal width so balances line up. Promo: the display face for a short title only, with a bold sans for the date and venue, in high-contrast text with an outline or shaded box, inside the safe zone.","ok":true,"fb":"Correct. The app needs legibility and aligned numbers; the promo needs one expressive title plus details that stay readable over moving footage and clear of the app's buttons."},{"t":"App: light grey text on white for a minimal look. Promo: white text with no outline over bright footage.","fb":"Both fail contrast. Banking information must be easy to read, and white text vanishes over bright video."},{"t":"App: a Didone serif at 12 px for elegance. Promo: a brush script for all the text, animated quickly.","fb":"Didone hairlines disappear at small screen sizes, and script text that moves quickly over video is almost unreadable."}]}
