      up: {"title":"Print layout or screen layout? (Challenge)","bloom":"Analyse","intro":"<p>The Saint Lucian studio's production checklist has more technical decisions. Sort each one by the medium it belongs to.</p>","items":[{"t":"A placed 300 ppi photo has been enlarged to 200%, so its effective resolution falls to 150 ppi; the designer finds a larger original.","bin":0,"fb":"Effective resolution at the printed size is a print concern."},{"t":"Exporting the hero image at twice its display width so it looks sharp on high-density phone screens.","bin":1,"fb":"High-density displays are a screen concern; only pixel dimensions matter there."},{"t":"Adding crop marks and exporting a PDF/X file for the printer.","bin":0,"fb":"Crop marks and PDF/X are print production standards."},{"t":"Choosing a 4:5 image so the post fills more of the Instagram feed.","bin":1,"fb":"Aspect ratios for a social feed are screen decisions."},{"t":"Checking a printed proof to see whether the turquoise logo still looks right on uncoated paper.","bin":0,"fb":"Paper changes how ink colours look, so print needs a proof."},{"t":"Making the \"Book a tour\" button large enough to tap easily with a thumb.","bin":1,"fb":"Tap targets are an interactive, screen concern."},{"t":"Placing page numbers and running heads on the master pages of each spread.","bin":0,"fb":"Folios and running heads on spreads belong to print editorial layout."},{"t":"Writing alt text for the waterfall photo.","bin":1,"fb":"Alt text is read by screen readers on the website."},{"t":"Testing the layout at 375 px wide to check that the three columns stack correctly.","bin":1,"fb":"Testing responsive behaviour at phone widths is a screen task."}],"win":"Well sorted. Print thinks in effective resolution, proofs, PDF/X and spreads; screens think in pixel density, aspect ratios, tap targets, alt text and responsive widths."}
